repo: charon
tier: strong
difficulty: 3
work_class: ci-infra
branch: feat/gate-integrity
depends_on:
owns: src/charon/gate_runner.py, tools/check_gate_registry.py, tools/check_inert_code.py, tools/inert_to_graph.py, tools/inert-code-disposition.json
note: |
  S1 of the CG remaining-work sequence. Full root-cause spec (file:line for every claim) at
  fleet/state/S1-GATE-INTEGRITY-SPEC.md — READ IT FIRST, do not re-derive. The "2 RED gates on
  master" framing was corrected: both pass on a fresh clone; the reds are LOCAL-tree pollution
  from ephemeral .claude/worktrees/agent-* copies swept into the inert AST scan (non-determinism).
  Do NOT edit tools/_vendor/ksf_inert_code.py (its header forbids hand-edits — fix via a
  monkeypatch of _EXCLUDE_DIRS from tools/check_inert_code.py).
accept: |
  ## Task (see S1-GATE-INTEGRITY-SPEC.md for the specified fix at each step)
  1. gate_runner.py: add pytest, check-decisions, render-review-log (--check, NOT bare — bare
     mutates docs/REVIEW-LOG.md) to CHECKS. check_gate_registry.py: ALL_DOMAINS += ci-infra,
     no-rig-import.
  2. FIRST fix determinism: extend _EXCLUDE_DIRS (via check_inert_code.py monkeypatch) to exclude
     .claude/ + caches. Verify: run `PYTHONPATH=src python3 tools/check_inert_code.py` 3x in a
     tree with .claude/worktrees/ present → identical counts + identical symbol lists all 3.
  3. tools/inert_to_graph.py (untracked): strip its stray `# @covers: inert-graph-coupling` line
     (it's a diagnostic tool, no invariant/exit-code contract) OR give it a real gates.json entry.
  4. inert-code-disposition.json: apply the §4 triage — DELETE ActualsLedger/ActualRow;
     keep-pending-wire (NOT delete) ReviewerCircuitBreaker/next_entry/proxy_excluded_keys;
     classify the rest per the spec table.

  ## Accept (all must pass)
  - PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m charon.cli gate  → GREEN (incl. the 3 newly-added checks)
  - PYTHONPATH=src python3 tools/check_inert_code.py  run 3x → deterministic, identical output
  - PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m pytest  → full suite green (incl. test_check_inert_code)

  ## Dependencies & sequence
  No depends_on. Disjoint from all live tickets except: shares no files with WORK-DECOMPOSER,
  FAIL-LOUD-CONTRACT (forwarder.py), or GRACEFUL-DEGRADE. Must LAND before those waves' verifies
  are trusted (a truthful gate is the prerequisite). Single wave.
